Howdy Next for Debian
=====================

This is an unofficial personal package. It does not enable PAM on
install. Test recognition before changing authentication.

After install
-------------

1. Identify a stable camera path under /dev/v4l/by-id/ or
   /dev/v4l/by-path/.
2. Run: sudo howdy config
   Set [video] device_path to that camera.
3. Run: sudo howdy download-models
4. Run: sudo howdy add
5. Run: sudo howdy test

PAM
---

Only add pam_howdy.so after "howdy test" works. See pam_howdy(8) and
https://codeberg.org/nathawat/howdy-next/wiki/PAM-Integration

Typical sudo/system-auth line (do not lock yourself out; keep a
password fallback):

  auth  sufficient  pam_howdy.so  workaround=native

Vendored OpenCV
---------------

Debian does not yet ship OpenCV 5 in main. This package includes a
private libopencv_world under /usr/lib/howdy-next so it does not
conflict with Debian's OpenCV 4.
